# Thousand Moons Infantry {2}{W} 2/4: "Untap this creature during each other player's untap step" (CR 502.3, 611.3a). Bot1 casts it and an Ornithopter on turn 1
# (Mox Pearl, Mox Ruby and Mox Jet pay exactly {2}{W}); on turn 3 both attack and stay tapped. In Bot2's untap step on turn 4 the Infantry untaps while
# Bot1's Ornithopter, which has no such rule, stays tapped. Bot2's own Ornithopter attacks on turn 4 and is still tapped in Bot1's turn 5 main phase:
# the rule lets the Infantry untap, not other creatures, and does not touch Bot2's permanents. On turn 5 both attack again, with the same result on turn 6.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Thousand Moons Infantry
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Thousand Moons Infantry.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Thousand Moons Infantry > Bot2; Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Thousand Moons Infantry.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Thousand Moons Infantry.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
Bot1.Attack(Thousand Moons Infantry > Bot2; Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T6 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Thousand Moons Infantry.Tapped = false
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = true
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Tapped = false
